  "preamble": "Loss of the voiced labiodental fricative [v] usually happens intervocalically or in consonant clusters, where the weak labial friction disappears. Middle English lost [v] (the voiced allophone of Old English f) in words like head and lord, Danish dropped it after /l/ (halv, selv), and Russian drops it in clusters such as здравствуйте.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Elision, Lenition, Cluster Simplification",
